  "cadence_deduction": "For fixed physical duration and half-life, independent thinning composes consistently. Poisson offspring of mean near1 retain order-one per-quantum variance every frame; the transient variance diverges approximately as1/frame_seconds when the frame shrinks. Matching mean retention alone therefore does not specify a consistent physical-time noise law.",
  "finite_time_variance_condition": "In this independent-branching reference, a near-identity offspring variance proportional to frame duration can avoid that divergence when m=1-lambda*frame_duration+O(frame_duration^2). This does not select a birth/death model or SDE.",
